# `zig build` output. Both are directories because a normal user build creates
# them, and a normal user build must not dirty this tree or leak into a package
# published from it.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Zig 0.16 materialises a fetched dependency into a project-local `zig-pkg/`
# beside the build root. This package declares no dependencies, so nothing
# creates it here today; the entry is here so that a future dependency cannot
# commit a fetched tree into the repository.
zig-pkg/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own output
# tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so that a build run
# from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# Upstream's own ignore rules are not restated here and not removed.
# libraries/liblmdb/.gitignore is upstream's, unmodified: it covers what
# liblmdb/Makefile drops beside its sources (mtest, mtest2..6, mdb_stat,
# mdb_copy, mdb_dump, mdb_load, mdb_drop, testdb, *.o, *.lo, *.a, *.so, *.exe,
# backup and editor droppings, gcov output, core dumps, valgrind output, and
# the man/ and html/ trees Doxygen writes). None of those patterns is broad
# enough to swallow a fork-owned path, so nothing above has to be re-included;
# the one pattern that could ever overlap, `*.a`, only matches the archive this
# build writes under zig-out/, which is ignored on its own account.
#
# This build never produces an upstream artifact in the source directory: it
# compiles the three core units (libraries/liblmdb/mdb.c, midl.c and
# module.c) and upstream's five installed tools from their own sources into
# zig-out, and `zig build interop` builds libraries/liblmdb/mdb_dump.c the same
# way. Upstream's `mdb_dump` pattern above is an exact name, so it would not
# have covered `mdb_dump.c` in any case, and nothing is ever written beside the
# sources.

# Development state, not source. `package.nix`, `flake.nix`, `devenv.nix`,
# `devenv.yaml` and `.envrc` at the package root are the standalone Nix and
# shell interface for this SDK, and the first four names below are what
# entering that shell or letting `direnv` in leaves beside them; the last two
# are what `nix build` leaves. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so a `zig fetch` consumer never receives one of them, and
# package.nix excludes the same names from its own source filter independently
# of this file. `libraries/liblmdb/.gitignore` is upstream's own, is left
# exactly as it is, and its bytes are a record in UPSTREAM.sha256.
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.state/
.direnv/
result
result-*